Subject: [PATCH 6/6] SystemUI: allow AOD sensor buckets to confirm dimming

Rothko can emit a new low bucket followed by high in 100 ms when relighting after brief extreme darkness. By the device backlight adapter both confirmed and transient low buckets are the same float. Keep confirmation at the point that owns sensor buckets and the subscription lifecycle.

Default to immediate updates with an empty interval table. On opted-in AOD use a cancellable wakeup alarm for a dimmer configured bucket. The first sample and unconfigured buckets remain immediate. Collect repeats without extending the deadline and cancel on superseding samples or listener removal.

Pinned upstream base: 22de88b7b8eb979c816669c7963dee66ae4953cd. Device-side configuration is required. Eight host scenarios using the production policy methods and AlarmTimeout passed. Full Android build and device acceptance pending.

